### Ordering Assistant - example API requests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client)
### Start the stack first: `make up`. All requests go through the API gateway.
@base = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Get a local dev token (local only; production uses your OIDC IdP)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/dev-token
Content-Type: application/json

{"user_id": "u-acme-buyer"}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 2. Ask for recommendations (starts a conversation)
# @name recs
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "What should I order for STORE-014?"}

###
@cid = {{recs.response.body.conversation_id}}

### 3. Explain a recommendation (grounded explanation + guideline citation)
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"conversation_id": "{{cid}}", "message": "Why is SKU-10042 recommended at STORE-014?"}

### 4. Propose an order → returns status=awaiting_approval + pending_approval
# @name proposal
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"conversation_id": "{{cid}}", "message": "Order it"}

### 5a. Confirm in chat (Idempotency-Key makes client retries safe)
# @name confirm
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: confirm-{{cid}}

{"conversation_id": "{{cid}}", "message": "yes"}

### 5b. …or approve/reject via the approvals API (e.g. an approver for high-value orders)
POST {{base}}/v1/approvals/{{proposal.response.body.pending_approval.approval_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"decision": "approve", "comment": "ok"}

### 6. Verify final status from the system of record
GET {{base}}/v1/orders/{{confirm.response.body.data.order.order_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Conversation transcript (+ any pending approval)
GET {{base}}/v1/conversations/{{cid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Policy question (RAG with citations)
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "What happens when a payment is declined?"}

### 9. Feedback on a reply (feeds the eval loop)
POST {{base}}/v1/conversations/{{cid}}/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"rating": 5, "labels": ["great_answer"], "comment": "clear explanation"}

### 10. Thread cache: stats, explicit cleanup, close conversation (clears cache)
GET {{base}}/v1/conversations/{{cid}}/cache
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{base}}/v1/conversations/{{cid}}/cache
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{base}}/v1/conversations/{{cid}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Long-term memory: list / erase everything (right to erasure)
GET {{base}}/v1/memory
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{base}}/v1/memory
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Recover a turn that failed mid-workflow
POST {{base}}/v1/conversations/{{cid}}/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Admin: audit trail and fault injection (non-production)
# @name admin
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/dev-token
Content-Type: application/json

{"user_id": "u-acme-admin"}

###
GET {{base}}/v1/audit?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}

###
POST {{base}}/v1/dev/faults
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"target": "payment", "mode": "unavailable", "ttl_s": 120}

###
POST {{base}}/v1/dev/faults
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"target": "payment", "mode": null}
